onal  roller coaster at times so we do have  our hobbies um and just just to be mates  and just be friends and just do fun  things um because the calendar can be so  demanding  and also you've known daniel for a long  time haven't you just tell us how long  have you known him how long have you  worked with him for  i've known him since i was 13. we've  been working together for just over four  years now so we do have that a bit of an  advantage to our you know on our side  especially during cover times and when  we are feeling homesick you know we are  mates so there are times where we just  be mates and and do fun stuff together  and just try and uh  i guess trying to ignore the the  external pressures of not being a c  family and uh and you know the demanding  nature of formula one itself fantastic  stuff thank you so much indeed for your  time michael italiano here's daniel  ricardo's performance  well with us this morning to review the  papers are the anthropologist marianna  hotter and the broadcaster gemma forte  and they join me now thank you very much  indeed it's good to see both of you  let's just kick off with um f1 actually  i've just been speaking to um one of our  guests on f1 which is very big day but  um  hamilton lewis hamilton and this whole  um talk of um links with grenfell i'll  come to you there um gemma just shed  some light on this for us  okay so it turns out that one of the  sponsors that was going to be all over  hamilton's car for branding wise as  kingspan now kingspan supplied the  combustible insulation that was on the  grenfell towers of course which that  tragedy was as recent as 2017 of course  and it's still extremely  raw and a very very sensitive subject  for so many reasons so there was a lot  of alarm a lot of dismay and um i do  understand louis hamilton he's in pole  position i'd imagine in this particular  sport as well it's so dangerous and the  focus is on the sport and yet it's a bit  disingenuous i think to sort of say o