hs of  kind of going well i've got this  headache  i've got mild  flu fluid cold symptoms don't know is  that covered is it a cough or a cold  that my kid picked up at school  some people are going ah maybe it's all  right it's probably not covered some  people don't maybe it is covered and  panicking  and obviously there's a knock-on  implication for how disruptive that is  for our  day-to-day lives uh the impact on on our  health care systems so perhaps a test  like this would be able to in one go  eliminate covid and also potentially  tell you what you do have so if it's  common cold then go home wrap up warm uh  paracetamol  you know a hot lemon drink and and you  know have an evening in um if it's  covered then obviously take the the  necessary precautions so this is very  exciting um and  you know hats off to our research  scientists once again  for leading us through uh this global  crisis absolutely my goodness are we so  thankful indeed um let me come to the  next story with you um gemma because  this is a story about storm irwin a week  on and so many people still don't have  any power and actually interestingly i  spoke to tim farron yesterday on this  program and he's the mp for westmoreland  and lonsdale and something that he said  he said if this had happened in  kensington for example then boris  johnson would have reacted quicker  what's your take on this  well quite possibly as you say if it  happened maybe in the home counties or  sorry  maybe he would have bothered to go there  i mean remember when we had the flooding  and and it took him days and days to to  bother going and i think it's when  you're you're talking about leveling up  as part of an agenda this really doesn't  show that you're taking that seriously  because this storm arwin and this  horrible outage of power has affected  thousands of homes in the northeast and  scotland  and when you think how cold it is at the  moment i mean i have to caveat this with  thinking about homeless peo